269	/// the track directly behind it — nothing (`none`, an ordinary track), or
270	/// cut it by their alpha, inverted alpha, Rec. 709 luma or inverted luma.
271	///
272	/// **The case ORDER is a shader discriminant** (MT-3): `shaderCode` is the
273	/// case index, `Compositor.metal`'s `kMatteNone`…`kMatteLumaInverted`
274	/// compare against the same integers, and the core declares the variants in
275	/// the same order. Append, never reorder — `BlendMode`'s rule.
276	enum TrackMatte: String, Codable, CaseIterable {
277	    case none
278	    case alpha
279	    case alphaInverted = "alpha_inverted"
280	    case luma
281	    case lumaInverted = "luma_inverted"
